Dapper Mapper's map viewing application, XViewSDTS, is ready for beta
testing.  Linux users in the US may find this a handy way to navigate
through map data provided by the United States Geological Survey (USGS).
The latest version, 0.05, adds the ability to overlay the USGS data with
your own objects to create custom maps.

This is not a full-blown Geographic Information System, but may be useful
for folks who enjoy working with topographic maps, and may want to create
simple maps for printing or including in a web page.

This product is currently unreleased, but Dapper Mapper is looking for
anyone who would like to try a free copy of the beta version and provide
some feedback.  If you think you might be interested, you may find more
information at http://www.dappermapper.com/products/xviewsdts/beta/

